"1\n00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:04,175\nThe Learning Brain. Series 7: Digital Learning\n\n2\n00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:07,333\nEpisode 2\n\n3\n00:00:07,413 --> 00:00:09,246\nCut the extras\n\n4\n00:00:12,046 --> 00:00:14,227\nA funny cartoon on a slide.\n\n5\n00:00:14,556 --> 00:00:17,071\nA dramatic story at the start of a lecture.\n\n6\n00:00:17,393 --> 00:00:19,479\nBackground music under a video.\n\n7\n00:00:19,727 --> 00:00:21,606\nThey make a lesson more interesting.\n\n8\n00:00:21,939 --> 00:00:23,562\nDo they make it more memorable?\n\n9\n00:00:23,732 --> 00:00:29,830\nMayer calls the principle coherence: people learn better when extraneous material is left out.\n\n10\n00:00:30,373 --> 00:00:32,528\nIn his 2021 summary,\n\n11\n00:00:32,714 --> 00:00:36,357\nthe median effect size was zero point eight six,\n\n12\n00:00:36,626 --> 00:00:39,416\npositive in eighteen of nineteen tests.\n\n13\n00:00:39,586 --> 00:00:44,420\nInteresting but irrelevant additions have a name: seductive details.\n\n14\n00:00:44,796 --> 00:00:53,625\nIn 2020, Kripa Sundararajan and Olusola Adesope pooled fifty eight studies with more than seventy five hundred students.\n\n15\n00:00:54,075 --> 00:00:58,765\nStudents who learned with seductive details did worse on learning measures.\n\n16\n00:00:58,935 --> 00:01:01,533\nThe harm was larger in short lessons,\n\n17\n00:01:01,753 --> 00:01:03,504\nfor students new to a topic,\n\n18\n00:01:03,877 --> 00:01:07,496\nand when the extra was placed right next to an important diagram.\n\n19\n00:01:08,041 --> 00:01:12,343\nThe authors also note that the overall effect was fairly small.\n\n20\n00:01:12,513 --> 00:01:13,029\nWhy?\n\n21\n00:01:13,141 --> 00:01:15,414\nAttention and working memory are limited.\n\n22\n00:01:15,897 --> 00:01:18,553\nA vivid detail can pull attention away,\n\n23\n00:01:18,793 --> 00:01:22,375\nand can even become the frame students remember the lesson by.\n\n24\n00:01:22,545 --> 00:01:23,924\nThere may be a trade off.\n\n25\n00:01:24,257 --> 00:01:27,606\nA joke can lower anxiety or build connection,\n\n26\n00:01:27,819 --> 00:01:32,502\nand researchers are studying whether those emotional benefits make up for the cost.\n\n27\n00:01:32,948 --> 00:01:34,762\nInterest is not the enemy.\n\n28\n00:01:35,068 --> 00:01:36,845\nIrrelevant interest is.\n\n29\n00:01:37,015 --> 00:01:37,781\nFor teaching.\n\n30\n00:01:38,142 --> 00:01:40,022\nBefore you add an image,\n\n31\n00:01:40,042 --> 00:01:43,243\nstory or sound, ask: does it explain the idea?\n\n32\n00:01:43,461 --> 00:01:44,287\nIf not, cut it,\n\n33\n00:01:44,307 --> 00:01:46,386\nor move it away from key content.\n\n34\n00:01:46,805 --> 00:01:47,825\nWhen you use a hook,\n\n35\n00:01:47,845 --> 00:01:50,053\nconnect it directly to the learning goal.\n\n36\n00:01:50,454 --> 00:01:52,309\nOne tip to share with students: when studying,\n\n37\n00:01:52,397 --> 00:01:54,945\nskip the tangents first.\n\n38\n00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:59,141\nMake it interesting, by making the idea itself interesting.\n\n"